 // (nvn_obj.h draw_rec): Breath of the Wild sums one scratch recording per mesh and per shape and render pass into each model's prerecorded commands, and with an
 // 8-byte BEGIN on each of several hundred recordings a model came out a 4 KB page over its resource size table entry
+// (nxkit 0024) One thread at a time records on a command buffer. A game's graphics contexts can share one (Super Mario Maker 2: every context starts on the same global buffer,
+// main+0x2e6f4c, and its Mii and picture jobs record on workers). On the Switch threads of one core with different priorities never run at once, so these recordings do not overlap;
+// here every guest thread runs in parallel, and two of them scribbled in one list ("BeginRecording re-entered", then a CALL record pointing at 0x1 or 0x3: a crash in the replay, or a
+// frozen picture). So a second thread's BeginRecording waits for the first one's EndRecording. A wait that outlasts REC_WAIT_S goes on as before, so this can't hang the game
+#define REC_MAX 256
+#define REC_WAIT_S 2
